## Lore

Outcasts serving a higher power, or puppets of an alien force? Not even the
Guardians fully understand what they are. Most appear to be men and women who
were transformed into supernatural beings and lost their memories in the
process. The transformation seems to be voluntary, because despite fading
memories and an uncertain future, most Guardians share a resolve to help and
protect humankind wherever they go.

They can heal and destroy with equal ease and are the bane of evil supernatural
beings, but they are not omnipotent. Having lost their pasts, they lack the
everyday and professional skills they once had and often rely on human friends,
followers or the charity of strangers. Their psychic powers let them see into
people''s souls, but their judgment is not infallible: some are naive, and others
grow self-righteous and intolerant. Most use their powers with moderation, avoid
claiming credit, and reveal their full power only when facing pure evil.

A Guardian looks like a small, pale human - about five feet tall, with sheet-white
skin, near-white hair, almost transparent gray, green or blue eyes, and smooth,
unwrinkled skin that makes them look child-like. Many disguise themselves with
wigs, dyes, make-up and colored contacts. Belying that look, they are incredibly
strong and resilient, and their most striking powers turn light into a weapon:
sunlight at midnight, blasts of pure energy that tear into supernatural beings,
and shields that stop bullets. They will kill if they must but nearly always seek
a non-lethal answer; evil supernatural beings - diabolic Nightbane, minions of
the Nightlords, true vampires - are destroyed out of hand.

## GM Notes

**Guardians as player characters.** A Guardian player character should remember
even less of its origins than a Nightbane. This book does not answer where they
come from, who made them or why, and the Game Master will need tentative answers
of his own. To some people they are angels, extraterrestrials or gods, met with
awe or adoration; others react with terror. Even positive feelings can bring
mobs of fanatical would-be followers seeking guidance, and a young Guardian has
little wisdom to offer. The disillusioned may attack them as the messengers of a
god who has abandoned them. They are not god-like problem-solvers; their one
constant is that they want to help others, selflessly.

**Precognitive senses.** Do not overuse this sense. It is best at the start of an
adventure, or in little flashes - sensing that someone needs help or that
something is not right - rather than spoon-feeding the plot.

**Alliances and allies.** Guardians often work with normal humans, many of whom
believe they are angels or benevolent extraterrestrials, and with practitioners
of magic, psychics and Nightbane who prove themselves dedicated enemies of the
Ba''al. Several Nightbane, and the odd Wampyr or Doppleganger, have joined an
independent group of Guardians or the Lightbringers.

**Average life span.** About four times a human''s; believed to be 300 to 400
years.

**Money.** Might have 2D4x10 dollars to start. As they make allies and are helped
by other Guardians, funds can rise to 2D6x100 dollars, usually spent on
necessities and helping others.

**Regular hangouts.** Soup kitchens, churches, temples, the biggest cities and
the worst slums; some keep a retreat or sanctuary in the wilderness or on a
mountain top to heal and meditate.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nb-guardian');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nb-guardian';

